WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:03.441 --> 00:00:06.651
- <font color="#D81D1D">Synced and corrected by VitoSilans</font> -
-- <font color="#138CE9">www.Addic7ed.com</font> --

2
00:00:06.653 --> 00:00:08.155
[Caws]

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

4
00:00:20.707 --> 00:00:22.588
Hey!

5
00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:23.589
Eh!

6
00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:24.751
Go!

7
00:00:28.715 --> 00:00:30.716
[Murmurs]

8
00:00:30.717 --> 00:00:33.049
[Thumping]

9
00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:34.100
[Clamor]

10
00:00:34.101 --> 00:00:36.012
[Sputtering]

11
00:00:36.013 --> 00:00:37.893
Good morning. Uncle Donald.

12
00:00:37.894 --> 00:00:40.686
You can't wear this
to your job interview.

13
00:00:40.687 --> 00:00:42.851
[Sputtering] My uniform!

14
00:00:42.854 --> 00:00:44.731
You gotta dress for the job you want.

15
00:00:44.734 --> 00:00:48.114
not the job you have. which is no job.

16
00:00:48.115 --> 00:00:50.616
Wah!

17
00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:53.869
Huey. don't touch the stove. It's hot!

18
00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:55.831
But it's a big day. and a big day

19
00:00:55.832 --> 00:00:57.847
calls for a big breakfast!

20
00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:00.076
[Deflating Sound]

21
00:01:00.077 --> 00:01:01.287
Bleh!

22
00:01:01.288 --> 00:01:03.919
I'll get the iron.

23
00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:06.172
Ouch! Ooch.

24
00:01:06.173 --> 00:01:08.634
[Sputtering]

25
00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:10.926
Stop helping me. And
put on your life vests!

26
00:01:10.927 --> 00:01:13.846
What if the boat goes down
while the babysitter's here?

27
00:01:13.849 --> 00:01:15.932
BOTH: Yes. Uncle Donald.

28
00:01:18.976 --> 00:01:21.357
Where is that babysitter?

29
00:01:21.358 --> 00:01:22.898
Where are you?!

30
00:01:22.899 --> 00:01:24.690
What?

31
00:01:24.691 --> 00:01:27.504
I didn't give you a new address.

32
00:01:27.507 --> 00:01:29.945
Well. what time can you get here?

33
00:01:29.946 --> 00:01:33.279
I... don't know.

34
00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:34.780
Crazy old bird.

35
00:01:34.781 --> 00:01:37.703
Where can I find another
babysitter at 10:00?

36
00:01:37.704 --> 00:01:39.786
- 10:00?!
- You gotta go!

37
00:01:40.877 --> 00:01:41.998
Aah!

38
00:01:41.999 --> 00:01:44.620
I can't just leave you!

39
00:01:44.621 --> 00:01:47.503
We can survive for a couple of hours!

40
00:01:47.504 --> 00:01:50.966
A couple of hours. Uh... well. okay.

41
00:01:50.967 --> 00:01:53.969
But just keep those life vests on!

42
00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:56.512
[Engine Starts]

43
00:01:56.513 --> 00:01:57.930
Where's Dewey?

44
00:01:57.933 --> 00:01:59.172
- Sleeping.
- Who's Dewey?

45
00:02:02.639 --> 00:02:04.850
Who's Dewey?

46
00:02:04.851 --> 00:02:07.813
All right. boys. we'll get
to Cape Suzette and back

47
00:02:07.814 --> 00:02:09.985
before anyone realizes we're gone.

48
00:02:09.986 --> 00:02:12.948
So long. Dorkburg! Hello...

49
00:02:12.949 --> 00:02:14.700
Uncle Donald?

50
00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.412
What... What's up?

51
00:02:16.413 --> 00:02:18.864
I can't leave you boys
alone for one minute!

52
00:02:18.865 --> 00:02:21.617
You were supposed to get
him out by 10:00. Hubert!

53
00:02:21.618 --> 00:02:24.960
You were supposed to signal before
you started the boat. Dewford!

54
00:02:24.961 --> 00:02:27.083
We never get to do anything!

55
00:02:27.084 --> 00:02:30.426
Boys. if we want to
keep our home afloat.

56
00:02:30.427 --> 00:02:34.630
we've all got to do
things we don't want to do.

57
00:02:34.631 --> 00:02:35.801
[Beeps]

58
00:02:35.802 --> 00:02:38.013
Destination: McDuck Manor.

59
00:02:38.014 --> 00:02:40.676
McDuck Manor? As in Scrooge McDuck?

60
00:02:40.677 --> 00:02:42.558
The bajillionaire?

61
00:02:42.559 --> 00:02:44.180
You're finally gonna sell us.

62
00:02:44.181 --> 00:02:47.773
I'm not gonna sell... He owes me.

63
00:02:47.774 --> 00:02:49.645
We're gonna meet Scrooge McDuck?

64
00:02:49.646 --> 00:02:51.147
- That guy's amazing!
- What!

65
00:02:51.148 --> 00:02:53.689
I heard he's so epic
he defeated a rock giant

66
00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:56.572
and carved a statue of
himself out of its legs!

67
00:02:56.573 --> 00:02:59.825
I heard he's so smart he solved
the mystery of the chupacabra.

68
00:02:59.826 --> 00:03:01.497
Turns out it was just a shaved bear!

69
00:03:01.498 --> 00:03:04.960
I heard that he's so rich
he only hunts for treasure

70
00:03:04.961 --> 00:03:07.042
to swim in it!

71
00:03:07.043 --> 00:03:09.705
All right. take it down a notch.

72
00:03:09.706 --> 00:03:11.757
It's only a couple of hours.

73
00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:16.011
A couple of hours with the
most exciting duck in the world!

74
00:03:16.012 --> 00:03:18.844
With business expanding
in the Spoonerville

75
00:03:18.845 --> 00:03:24.140
and St. Canard markets. noted
in Appendices C. G and 5F.

76
00:03:24.141 --> 00:03:27.062
we're also cutting funding
to unnecessary departments:

77
00:03:27.063 --> 00:03:29.485
Historical Research. Experimental Tech.

78
00:03:29.486 --> 00:03:31.147
Deep Sea Exploration...

79
00:03:31.148 --> 00:03:33.135
Fantastic.

80
00:03:38.865 --> 00:03:40.536
Back in the bin with ya.

81
00:03:40.537 --> 00:03:42.738
See you tomorrow. [Sighs]

82
00:03:42.739 --> 00:03:43.660
[Clinks]

83
00:03:48.665 --> 00:03:50.207
[Grunting]

84
00:03:59.256 --> 00:04:03.098
[Tires Squealing]

85
00:04:03.099 --> 00:04:04.431
[Barking]

86
00:04:05.852 --> 00:04:09.185
Just another day at
the office. eh. Mr. McD?

87
00:04:09.186 --> 00:04:10.726
[Laughs] Been there.

88
00:04:10.727 --> 00:04:12.358
I don't have an office. per se.

89
00:04:12.359 --> 00:04:15.150
but in some ways the road is my office.

90
00:04:15.151 --> 00:04:18.774
Hey. that's deep. I
gotta write that down.

91
00:04:18.775 --> 00:04:20.947
[Crash]

92
00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:25.371
Geh! Eyes on the road. McQuack!

93
00:04:25.372 --> 00:04:27.783
Every dent is coming out of your salary.

94
00:04:27.784 --> 00:04:30.125
Absolutely. Hey. ya read about

95
00:04:30.126 --> 00:04:33.128
that crazy snowstorm on
the Drake Barrier Reef?

96
00:04:33.129 --> 00:04:35.284
I'd hate to fly into that one.

97
00:04:35.287 --> 00:04:38.924
See. I'm a bit of a
pilot. and. uh... Oh. okay.

98
00:04:38.925 --> 00:04:41.428
Divider... there you go.

99
00:04:44.641 --> 00:04:46.516
Hit the brakes!

100
00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:47.730
[Tires Squealing]

101
00:04:48.912 --> 00:04:49.912
Ech.

102
00:04:49.915 --> 00:04:51.036
Why aren't we moving?

103
00:04:51.039 --> 00:04:52.978
Mrs. B.. open up!

104
00:04:52.979 --> 00:04:54.810
I need to get out of here before...

105
00:04:54.811 --> 00:04:56.071
[Honking]

106
00:04:56.072 --> 00:04:57.943
he shows up.

107
00:04:57.944 --> 00:04:59.985
Hey! Jettison that jalopy

108
00:04:59.986 --> 00:05:03.410
from my driveway this
instant. ya deadbeat!

109
00:05:08.585 --> 00:05:10.246
Donald Duck.

110
00:05:10.247 --> 00:05:11.827
Uncle Scrooge.

111
00:05:11.828 --> 00:05:17.464
- Uncle Scrooge!
- [All Jeering]

112
00:05:19.709 --> 00:05:22.007
So. you're looking good.

113
00:05:22.008 --> 00:05:24.840
Still living on that boat?

114
00:05:24.841 --> 00:05:27.844
Yup. Still a trillionaire?

115
00:05:28.805 --> 00:05:30.686
[Bird Calls]

116
00:05:30.687 --> 00:05:32.642
Good. good.

117
00:05:32.645 --> 00:05:33.775
So...

118
00:05:33.856 --> 00:05:35.437
So...

119
00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:37.152
Jettison that jalopy

120
00:05:37.153 --> 00:05:40.946
from my driveway this
instant. you deadbeat!

121
00:05:40.947 --> 00:05:42.220
Oh. here we go!

122
00:05:42.223 --> 00:05:45.361
Giving orders like he's the
richest duck in the world!

123
00:05:45.362 --> 00:05:47.243
I am the richest duck in the world!

124
00:05:47.244 --> 00:05:48.244
Now move!

125
00:05:48.245 --> 00:05:49.665
I would love to!

126
00:05:49.666 --> 00:05:51.957
It just so happens I
have a job interview.

127
00:05:51.958 --> 00:05:53.999
So why are you standing there yelling?

128
00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.582
Mrs. B. said that you
would watch the boys!

129
00:05:56.583 --> 00:05:59.214
Can you do that without losing them?!

130
00:05:59.215 --> 00:06:01.297
- Of course I can!
- Fantastic!

131
00:06:01.298 --> 00:06:04.049
Thank you so much!

132
00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:05.841
You're welcome! Wait. what now?

133
00:06:05.842 --> 00:06:07.142
[Car Door Slams]

134
00:06:07.143 --> 00:06:10.346
Huey. Dewey. Louie. meet Scrooge McDuck.

135
00:06:10.347 --> 00:06:13.849
Remember. no tricks.
no lies. no trouble.

136
00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:15.941
ALL: Yes. Uncle Donald.

137
00:06:15.942 --> 00:06:18.024
I wasn't talking to you.

138
00:06:35.872 --> 00:06:37.464
Whoa!

139
00:06:40.377 --> 00:06:43.009
Talk to your nephews.

140
00:06:45.131 --> 00:06:46.843
Ew.

141
00:06:48.345 --> 00:06:49.725
[Startles]

142
00:06:49.726 --> 00:06:54.560
So. do children still
like marbles or...?

143
00:06:54.561 --> 00:06:55.649
Are you really our uncle?

144
00:06:55.652 --> 00:06:57.693
- How old are you?
- What's your net worth?

145
00:06:57.694 --> 00:06:58.934
What's the deal with
you and Uncle Donald?

146
00:06:58.935 --> 00:07:00.607
Is that fork real silver? Can I have it?

147
00:07:00.610 --> 00:07:03.315
- How come you never visit?
- 'Cause you're so old and moving is so hard?

148
00:07:03.317 --> 00:07:05.320
You owe us. like. a lot
of birthday presents.

149
00:07:05.321 --> 00:07:09.365
You used to be a big deal!
Whatever happened to you?

150
00:07:09.366 --> 00:07:11.036
Beakley!

151
00:07:11.037 --> 00:07:12.442
Aah!

152
00:07:12.445 --> 00:07:13.949
You agreed to watch them.

153
00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:15.621
Watch them.

154
00:07:15.622 --> 00:07:18.892
Huey. Louie. the third one...

155
00:07:21.838 --> 00:07:25.461
Please do not leave the
designated play area.

156
00:07:25.462 --> 00:07:27.803
- [Clinks]
- A gift from your great-uncle.

157
00:07:27.804 --> 00:07:29.595
You will return them
upon your departure.

158
00:07:29.596 --> 00:07:31.927
He's counted them.

159
00:07:31.928 --> 00:07:33.018
[Lock Clicks]

160
00:07:33.019 --> 00:07:35.140
Great. Now we've got two boring uncles.

161
00:07:35.141 --> 00:07:37.272
So. we're totally
ditching this room. right?

162
00:07:37.273 --> 00:07:40.776
Yup. and I know just how to do it.

163
00:07:40.777 --> 00:07:41.858
[Gasps]

164
00:07:51.698 --> 00:07:53.579
[Grumbling]

165
00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:56.582
"Used to be a big deal."

166
00:07:56.583 --> 00:07:58.123
[Beating]

167
00:07:58.124 --> 00:08:01.046
Stupid doorknob. come off!

168
00:08:01.047 --> 00:08:02.167
Nailed it!

169
00:08:02.168 --> 00:08:04.209
Can't believe that was your best plan.

170
00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:08.303
Come on. guys. let's go
touch some expensive stuff.

171
00:08:08.304 --> 00:08:11.006
- Aah!
- Dewey!

172
00:08:11.007 --> 00:08:12.599
BOTH: Aah!

173
00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:16.141
I'll put the marbles back. I swear!

174
00:08:16.142 --> 00:08:19.184
Who sent you? Ma Beagle? Glomgold?

175
00:08:19.185 --> 00:08:20.275
Answer me!

176
00:08:20.276 --> 00:08:24.900
[Sobbing] Uncle Scrooge!

177
00:08:24.901 --> 00:08:26.361
Uncle Scrooge?

178
00:08:26.362 --> 00:08:29.234
Oh. my gosh. the nephews!

179
00:08:29.235 --> 00:08:32.407
- Wait. you know us?
- [Grunting]

180
00:08:32.408 --> 00:08:36.031
Of course! Researching Mr. McDuck
and his family is kind of my hobby.

181
00:08:36.032 --> 00:08:38.123
- What?
- What are your blood types?

182
00:08:38.124 --> 00:08:40.371
What's Donald really like?
Who's the evil triplet?

183
00:08:40.374 --> 00:08:41.624
- Louie.
- Eh.

184
00:08:41.627 --> 00:08:43.588
Tell me everything!

185
00:08:43.591 --> 00:08:45.631
Um. we live with our uncle?

186
00:08:45.632 --> 00:08:47.002
On a boat?

187
00:08:47.003 --> 00:08:48.424
Go on.

188
00:08:48.425 --> 00:08:49.417
Kinda it.

189
00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.384
We're just a normal. boring family.

190
00:08:51.387 --> 00:08:54.389
Normal. boring? Hah!

191
00:08:54.390 --> 00:08:56.812
ALL: Ohh!

192
00:08:56.813 --> 00:08:59.224
Whoa!

193
00:08:59.225 --> 00:09:01.056
Huey. Dewey. and Louie Duck.

194
00:09:01.057 --> 00:09:03.479
Scrooge McDuck's great-nephews
on his sister Hortense's side

195
00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.020
with Quackmore Duck twice removed!

196
00:09:05.021 --> 00:09:06.982
And you are?

197
00:09:06.983 --> 00:09:09.194
Oh. right. Webby van der Quack.

198
00:09:09.195 --> 00:09:10.696
My granny's the housekeeper.

199
00:09:10.697 --> 00:09:13.158
Wait! Are we... friends now?

200
00:09:13.159 --> 00:09:15.070
If we say yes. will you let us live?

201
00:09:15.071 --> 00:09:17.073
[Scoffs] Good one. new best friend!

202
00:09:20.286 --> 00:09:24.339
So. friend. what do you
do for fun around here?

203
00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:26.131
Oh! I'm the best at fun.

204
00:09:26.132 --> 00:09:28.384
Um... yah!

205
00:09:30.216 --> 00:09:32.588
At least it's not the marble room.

206
00:09:32.589 --> 00:09:35.181
[Grunting]

207
00:09:39.516 --> 00:09:41.647
Come on. you blaggert.

208
00:09:41.648 --> 00:09:44.149
You won't get the
best of Scrooge McDuck!

209
00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:46.101
Hmm. A little spring cleaning?

210
00:09:46.102 --> 00:09:48.485
Maybe. Maybe not. Read this.

211
00:09:49.486 --> 00:09:52.107
Snow on the Drake Barrier Reef.

212
00:09:52.108 --> 00:09:54.029
First time in 50 years.

213
00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:56.071
That weather report aligns perfectly

214
00:09:56.072 --> 00:09:57.913
with the Papia Prophecy.

215
00:09:57.914 --> 00:10:03.118
A shift in currents may
present a pathway to Atlantis.

216
00:10:03.119 --> 00:10:05.881
lost city under the sea!

217
00:10:05.882 --> 00:10:08.544
This is because some children
made fun of you. isn't it?

218
00:10:08.545 --> 00:10:12.007
Nonsense! I'm no has-been.
They're the has-beens.

219
00:10:12.008 --> 00:10:13.969
I am an am-now.

220
00:10:13.970 --> 00:10:15.090
Make a list!

221
00:10:15.091 --> 00:10:16.431
Four oxygen tanks.

222
00:10:16.432 --> 00:10:18.133
two pressure gauges. a pilot...

223
00:10:18.134 --> 00:10:20.095
- I'm a pilot.
- A week's provisions.

224
00:10:20.096 --> 00:10:22.267
- an experimental deep-sea sub...
- I'm a pilot.

225
00:10:22.268 --> 00:10:24.309
And one secretary for an old man

226
00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:28.234
who seems to have forgotten
that I am not his secretary!

227
00:10:29.906 --> 00:10:33.699
So. eh. not interested?

228
00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:36.031
I have enough excitement
caring for Webby.

229
00:10:36.032 --> 00:10:38.704
Perhaps you should spend
some time with your family.

230
00:10:38.705 --> 00:10:43.288
Oh. hang up my spats. become the
doddering old relic everyone thinks I am.

231
00:10:43.289 --> 00:10:45.661
spinning yarns to those
loud-mouth young'uns

232
00:10:45.662 --> 00:10:47.252
about the man I used to be?

233
00:10:47.253 --> 00:10:50.425
You have avoided them for ten years!

234
00:10:50.426 --> 00:10:53.879
Because family is nothing but trouble!

235
00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:56.172
[Gasps] Oh.

236
00:10:57.473 --> 00:10:59.094
I'm Scrooge McDuck.

237
00:10:59.095 --> 00:11:01.887
I made my name being
tougher than the toughies

238
00:11:01.888 --> 00:11:03.809
and smarter than the smarties.

239
00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:06.942
And I made my money square. on my own.

240
00:11:06.943 --> 00:11:10.185
no nephews. no family.
no one helped me there.

241
00:11:10.186 --> 00:11:12.187
and I don't need help now. and...

242
00:11:12.188 --> 00:11:14.149
[Clattering]

243
00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:15.692
Beakley. a little help.

244
00:11:19.407 --> 00:11:21.157
Maybe they're right.

245
00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:26.121
Whoo! Vent crawl!

246
00:11:26.122 --> 00:11:27.583
[Both Groan]

247
00:11:27.584 --> 00:11:29.625
You don't get out much. do you?

248
00:11:29.626 --> 00:11:31.877
Eh. Granny's a bit overprotective.

249
00:11:31.878 --> 00:11:33.969
She trains me to be ready for anything.

250
00:11:33.970 --> 00:11:36.301
but then she says I've got
everything I need in here.

251
00:11:36.302 --> 00:11:39.174
But one day. I'm gonna see the world.

252
00:11:39.175 --> 00:11:43.308
I'm gonna be an explorer!
I'm gonna eat a hamburger.

253
00:11:43.309 --> 00:11:45.220
We could bring you a hamburger.

254
00:11:45.221 --> 00:11:47.143
You really are my best friends.

255
00:11:50.774 --> 00:11:54.781
Welcome to the Wing of Secrets!

256
00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:05.540
I knew it!

257
00:12:05.541 --> 00:12:07.242
Dewey. check it out!

258
00:12:07.243 --> 00:12:09.955
Yeah. whatever.

259
00:12:09.956 --> 00:12:12.377
The Gong of Picchu.

260
00:12:12.380 --> 00:12:17.305
Hit it three times to
unleash unspeakable evil.

261
00:12:20.016 --> 00:12:21.466
Uh. what are you doing?

262
00:12:21.467 --> 00:12:23.639
Calling dibs on stuff!

263
00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:26.391
What? Scrooge is. like.
he's. like. super old.

264
00:12:26.392 --> 00:12:28.473
Oh. careful! Medusa gauntlet.

265
00:12:28.474 --> 00:12:31.566
One touch can turn
organic matter to stone.

266
00:12:31.567 --> 00:12:33.398
[Imitates Solidifying]

267
00:12:33.399 --> 00:12:35.230
I'm gonna call this one a maybe.

268
00:12:35.231 --> 00:12:37.272
This place is incredible!

269
00:12:37.273 --> 00:12:38.484
It's fake.

270
00:12:41.868 --> 00:12:43.989
Is that Uncle Donald?

271
00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:46.621
Oh. yeah. he was Mr. McDuck's sidekick!

272
00:12:46.622 --> 00:12:49.374
- Dewey's right.
- Totally fake.

273
00:12:49.375 --> 00:12:51.546
Uncle Donald has never
done anything cool.

274
00:12:51.547 --> 00:12:56.882
What? Donald Duck is one of the
most daring adventurers of all time!

275
00:12:56.883 --> 00:12:59.054
[Stuttering]

276
00:12:59.055 --> 00:13:01.096
[Phone Rings]

277
00:13:01.097 --> 00:13:02.348
[Shiny Ring]

278
00:13:06.763 --> 00:13:08.303
Bop bop.

279
00:13:08.304 --> 00:13:10.065
Bop.

280
00:13:10.066 --> 00:13:11.516
Yo. chung chung!

281
00:13:11.517 --> 00:13:12.858
Bop bop!

282
00:13:12.859 --> 00:13:16.903
[Exclaiming]

283
00:13:19.525 --> 00:13:22.198
[Yelling]

284
00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:25.530
This has got to be a fake.

285
00:13:25.531 --> 00:13:27.662
And I bet everything else is. too.

286
00:13:27.663 --> 00:13:29.084
That's not true!

287
00:13:29.085 --> 00:13:31.376
What about this picture with chupacabra?

288
00:13:31.377 --> 00:13:34.499
- Photoshop.
- This treasure chest?

289
00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:36.501
Probably bought it at an auction.

290
00:13:36.502 --> 00:13:39.424
This... g-ghost?

291
00:13:39.425 --> 00:13:42.598
You mean this Halloween decoration?

292
00:13:45.471 --> 00:13:48.393
Curse ye. ye scurvy life-lubbers!

293
00:13:48.394 --> 00:13:51.726
It's Captain Peghook. the
scourge of the River Styx!

294
00:13:51.727 --> 00:13:55.270
It's real. It's really. really real!

295
00:13:55.271 --> 00:13:56.651
[Evil Laughter]

296
00:13:56.652 --> 00:13:58.523
The Deus Excalibur!

297
00:13:58.524 --> 00:14:00.615
It won't rest until its target's slain!

298
00:14:00.616 --> 00:14:03.278
But he's already dead!

299
00:14:03.279 --> 00:14:05.700
[Gong Rings]

300
00:14:05.701 --> 00:14:08.363
[Gasps] Do not let
anything else hit that gong!

301
00:14:08.364 --> 00:14:10.455
Yep. I'm gonna sit this one out.

302
00:14:10.456 --> 00:14:12.167
- Whoa! Aah!
- [Whinnies]

303
00:14:12.168 --> 00:14:13.458
[Exclaims]

304
00:14:13.459 --> 00:14:15.500
The headless man-horse!

305
00:14:15.501 --> 00:14:17.422
That one feels self-explanatory.

306
00:14:17.423 --> 00:14:19.374
[Rings]

307
00:14:19.375 --> 00:14:20.585
That's twice!

308
00:14:20.586 --> 00:14:23.048
One more. and something
terrible could happen!

309
00:14:23.049 --> 00:14:25.017
What could be worse than this?

310
00:14:25.020 --> 00:14:28.383
What in dismal downs
is going on in here?

311
00:14:28.384 --> 00:14:31.187
ALL: There it is.

312
00:14:33.689 --> 00:14:35.440
Why aren't you in your rooms?

313
00:14:35.441 --> 00:14:36.892
[Screaming]

314
00:14:36.893 --> 00:14:38.103
Rrrawgh!

315
00:14:38.104 --> 00:14:40.605
- Aah!
- [Evil Laughter]

316
00:14:40.606 --> 00:14:42.398
[Grunts]

317
00:14:43.699 --> 00:14:44.951
[Neighs]

318
00:14:48.364 --> 00:14:49.614
We've got this.

319
00:14:49.615 --> 00:14:51.406
There are four of us and three of them.

320
00:14:51.407 --> 00:14:53.458
If we... wait. never
mind. They teamed up.

321
00:14:53.459 --> 00:14:55.500
[Evil Laughter]

322
00:14:55.501 --> 00:14:58.083
Ah. good. that means only one target.

323
00:14:58.084 --> 00:15:00.335
No. get back! You're old!

324
00:15:00.336 --> 00:15:05.010
Oi. beastie! What's it gonna take
to shuffle you off to the afterlife?

325
00:15:05.011 --> 00:15:08.803
The head of Scrooge McDuck!

326
00:15:08.804 --> 00:15:10.555
[Cracking]

327
00:15:10.556 --> 00:15:13.428
Would you settle for his hat?

328
00:15:13.429 --> 00:15:14.350
[Roaring]

329
00:15:16.192 --> 00:15:17.894
[Groans]

330
00:15:22.488 --> 00:15:24.490
[Blade Rings]

331
00:15:26.032 --> 00:15:28.444
There's your head.

332
00:15:29.996 --> 00:15:33.749
I should've been more specific!

333
00:15:42.048 --> 00:15:43.548
[Whinnies]

334
00:15:43.549 --> 00:15:47.512
[Celebrating]

335
00:15:47.513 --> 00:15:48.884
[Pounds]

336
00:15:48.885 --> 00:15:50.555
We can explain.

337
00:15:50.556 --> 00:15:53.518
We came down to your secret
museum to look for you.

338
00:15:53.519 --> 00:15:56.231
because we love you?

339
00:15:56.232 --> 00:15:58.063
Secret museum?

340
00:15:58.064 --> 00:15:59.855
This is the gar-age!

341
00:16:01.567 --> 00:16:02.647
The what?

342
00:16:02.648 --> 00:16:04.239
Do you mean "garage"?

343
00:16:04.240 --> 00:16:05.860
No. that's ridiculous.

344
00:16:05.861 --> 00:16:08.613
If this is a garage.
then how do you explain

345
00:16:08.614 --> 00:16:10.485
all this amazing stuff?

346
00:16:10.486 --> 00:16:13.538
Like the garden hose of destiny?

347
00:16:13.539 --> 00:16:16.491
Or Montezuma's stack of old magazines?

348
00:16:16.492 --> 00:16:20.045
Or... Oh. yeah. it's a garage.

349
00:16:20.046 --> 00:16:23.378
Unbelievable. I invite
you into my home...

350
00:16:23.379 --> 00:16:25.210
You locked us in a room!

351
00:16:25.211 --> 00:16:26.501
I gave you marbles!

352
00:16:26.502 --> 00:16:28.173
All we wanted was to hand out with you!

353
00:16:28.174 --> 00:16:29.424
Well. now you have.

354
00:16:29.425 --> 00:16:30.885
and look at the mess it's got me!

355
00:16:30.886 --> 00:16:34.719
I guess family is nothing
but trouble. right. Scrooge?

356
00:16:35.713 --> 00:16:37.913
Everybody out!

357
00:16:37.916 --> 00:16:39.724
- But we're...
- Out!

358
00:16:39.725 --> 00:16:42.017
Well. what are you gaping at?

359
00:16:42.018 --> 00:16:44.940
The curse is only activated if
you ring the gong three times

360
00:16:44.941 --> 00:16:48.153
and... you already hit
it two times. didn't you?

361
00:16:48.154 --> 00:16:49.365
[Crackling]

362
00:16:56.475 --> 00:16:59.534
Pixiu. the Gold-Hunting Dragon...

363
00:16:59.535 --> 00:17:01.242
Gold hunting? Sounds great!

364
00:17:01.245 --> 00:17:04.749
Not when you're Duckburg's
single largest owner of gold!

365
00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:06.381
[Sniffing]

366
00:17:06.382 --> 00:17:08.594
Aah! Me money bin!

367
00:17:10.636 --> 00:17:13.086
To your rooms!

368
00:17:18.144 --> 00:17:19.644
Where are you going?

369
00:17:19.645 --> 00:17:22.437
I'm gonna go eat a hamburger!

370
00:17:22.438 --> 00:17:24.019
We're in!

371
00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:25.730
Cool.

372
00:17:25.731 --> 00:17:27.562
To be clear. I'm gonna
go catch the dragon.

373
00:17:27.563 --> 00:17:29.402
The hamburger was a
metaphor from before.

374
00:17:29.405 --> 00:17:31.076
Yeah. yeah. no. we get it. We get it.

375
00:17:31.079 --> 00:17:33.118
But how are we gonna get up there?

376
00:17:33.119 --> 00:17:34.330
I'm a pilot.

377
00:17:43.789 --> 00:17:45.710
Ooh! Yeah! Ha ha!

378
00:17:45.711 --> 00:17:48.463
It'll take more than some fancy flying

379
00:17:48.464 --> 00:17:52.347
to shake old Scrooge.
you cash cannibal! Whoo!

380
00:17:52.348 --> 00:17:55.551
Oh! Ow! Ugh!

381
00:17:56.852 --> 00:17:59.724
It'll take more than a bruised spine

382
00:17:59.725 --> 00:18:01.726
to shake old Scrooge.

383
00:18:01.727 --> 00:18:03.899
you bad dragon-dog!

384
00:18:09.065 --> 00:18:11.317
Take that!

385
00:18:13.569 --> 00:18:17.018
No!

386
00:18:22.078 --> 00:18:23.959
[Straining]

387
00:18:26.292 --> 00:18:27.502
Whoo-hoo!

388
00:18:27.503 --> 00:18:29.584
I thought I told you to go to your...

389
00:18:29.585 --> 00:18:30.885
No time. We gotta work fast.

390
00:18:30.886 --> 00:18:32.887
Webby. how do we stop it?

391
00:18:32.888 --> 00:18:35.220
It's mystical. so we
need a mystical device.

392
00:18:35.221 --> 00:18:38.343
like an oblivion mirror
or a medusa gauntlet. or...

393
00:18:38.344 --> 00:18:40.515
- Like this?
- Grr.

394
00:18:40.516 --> 00:18:42.228
What? I was gonna give it back.

395
00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:46.691
Now. how do we get him down there?

396
00:18:46.692 --> 00:18:48.643
Garden hose of destiny!

397
00:18:48.644 --> 00:18:50.945
Launchpad. we need to swing him out.

398
00:18:50.946 --> 00:18:53.778
Nosedive towards the bin
and get ready to pull up!

399
00:18:53.779 --> 00:18:55.491
Yes. sir. random kid I just met!

400
00:18:57.743 --> 00:19:01.286
- Any questions?
- Since when is Launchpad a pilot?

401
00:19:01.287 --> 00:19:02.658
[Clinks]

402
00:19:09.665 --> 00:19:12.758
You guys. our family is awesome!

403
00:19:19.515 --> 00:19:20.766
ALL: Scrooge!

404
00:19:33.739 --> 00:19:34.740
[Gasping]

405
00:19:37.653 --> 00:19:39.654
[Cheering]

406
00:19:39.655 --> 00:19:41.746
NEPHEW: Money! I knew it!

407
00:19:41.747 --> 00:19:45.160
Aw. Family truly is the
greatest adventure of...

408
00:19:45.161 --> 00:19:46.911
Oh. no. the ground!

409
00:19:46.912 --> 00:19:47.963
[Crashing]

410
00:19:50.756 --> 00:19:52.877
In the short time I've known you.

411
00:19:52.878 --> 00:19:55.090
you've wrecked my home and my money bin.

412
00:19:55.091 --> 00:19:57.509
unleashed several ancient evils.

413
00:19:57.512 --> 00:20:00.173
and almost got me killed. twice.

414
00:20:00.176 --> 00:20:03.678
Four times if you count each
monster as an individual time...

415
00:20:03.679 --> 00:20:09.104
[Laughter]

416
00:20:09.105 --> 00:20:11.106
That was incredible!

417
00:20:11.107 --> 00:20:12.727
When you pulled me into the airplane

418
00:20:12.728 --> 00:20:14.319
and said "No time!"

419
00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:15.730
And who would have thought

420
00:20:15.731 --> 00:20:17.902
of a Medusa Gauntlet?! Brilliant!

421
00:20:17.903 --> 00:20:19.864
Oh. and then you swung me out

422
00:20:19.865 --> 00:20:22.287
and pulled up just
in time and [Laughter]

423
00:20:22.288 --> 00:20:24.739
You kids are nothing but trouble!

424
00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:28.873
Curse me kilts. have I missed trouble!

425
00:20:28.874 --> 00:20:32.127
I suppose I'll have
to keep an eye on you

426
00:20:32.128 --> 00:20:35.590
to teach you how to get
into trouble properly.

427
00:20:35.591 --> 00:20:37.051
- [Phone Ringing]
- You mean...?

428
00:20:37.052 --> 00:20:39.174
Beakley! Clear my schedule!

429
00:20:39.175 --> 00:20:42.177
I'm taking the wee ones on a field trip.

430
00:20:42.178 --> 00:20:45.890
About time. And once again.
I am not your secre...

431
00:20:45.891 --> 00:20:50.565
Now. let's go find the
lost city of Atlantis!

432
00:20:50.566 --> 00:20:51.896
ALL: Yeah!

433
00:20:51.897 --> 00:20:54.819
And no one tell your uncle Donald!

434
00:20:54.820 --> 00:20:56.231
ALL: Yeah!

435
00:20:56.232 --> 00:20:58.032
Who is that?

436
00:20:58.033 --> 00:20:59.614
[Struggling]

437
00:20:59.615 --> 00:21:00.905
You've got the job. Duck!

438
00:21:00.906 --> 00:21:02.407
Seriously?

439
00:21:02.408 --> 00:21:03.778
Oh. boy!

440
00:21:03.779 --> 00:21:05.870
I'm a real accountant!

441
00:21:05.871 --> 00:21:08.283
Accountant? That was filled yesterday.

442
00:21:08.284 --> 00:21:10.286
You're our new sailor!

443
00:21:12.288 --> 00:21:14.959
Welcome to Glomgold Industries!

444
00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:19.351
Now. what do you know about Atlantis?

445
00:21:23.469 --> 00:21:26.561
♪ Life is like a hurricane ♪

446
00:21:26.562 --> 00:21:29.013
♪ Here in Duckburg ♪

447
00:21:29.014 --> 00:21:31.806
♪ Racecars. laser. airplanes ♪

448
00:21:31.807 --> 00:21:34.479
♪ It's a Duckburg ♪

449
00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:36.981
♪ We might solve the mystery ♪

450
00:21:36.982 --> 00:21:39.574
♪ We'll rewrite history ♪

451
00:21:39.575 --> 00:21:41.866
♪ Ducktales ♪

452
00:21:41.867 --> 00:21:45.630
♪ Every day they're out
there making ducktales ♪

453
00:21:45.633 --> 00:21:46.844
♪ Whoo-ooh ♪

454
00:21:46.847 --> 00:21:48.913
♪ Tales of daring-do ♪

455
00:21:48.914 --> 00:21:52.287
♪ And good-luck tales ♪

456
00:21:52.288 --> 00:21:55.330
♪ T-t-t-teaser grows behind you ♪

457
00:21:55.331 --> 00:21:58.002
♪ Got a stranger out to find you ♪

458
00:21:58.003 --> 00:22:01.546
♪ What to do. just climb
onto some ducktales ♪

459
00:22:01.547 --> 00:22:03.258
♪ Whoo-ooh ♪

460
00:22:03.259 --> 00:22:08.052
♪ Every day they're out
there making ducktales ♪

461
00:22:08.053 --> 00:22:10.832
♪ Tales of tarries bad and good ♪

462
00:22:10.835 --> 00:22:15.231
♪ Not phony tales so
come into the Ducktales ♪

463
00:22:21.357 --> 00:22:23.818
Glomgold Industries!

464
00:22:23.819 --> 00:22:26.241
Take an idea.

465
00:22:26.242 --> 00:22:27.662
Make it your own.

466
00:22:27.663 --> 00:22:30.706
Better. faster. cheaper.

467
00:22:31.997 --> 00:22:33.457
That's the motto

468
00:22:33.460 --> 00:22:37.001
of the world's most beloved
Scottish billionaire duck!

469
00:22:37.002 --> 00:22:40.425
Flintheart Glomgold!

470
00:22:40.426 --> 00:22:42.587
Welcome. new employees.

471
00:22:42.588 --> 00:22:44.088
to Glomgold Industries.

472
00:22:44.089 --> 00:22:45.880
where our employees

473
00:22:45.881 --> 00:22:50.015
are the greatest treasure of all!

474
00:22:51.186 --> 00:22:52.847
[Clapping]

475
00:22:52.848 --> 00:22:54.939
Glomgold! Glomgold!

476
00:22:54.940 --> 00:22:56.981
Glom... Fine.

477
00:22:56.982 --> 00:22:58.853
Enough glad-handing.

478
00:22:58.854 --> 00:23:01.606
You're here because you're
the best of the cheapest.

479
00:23:01.607 --> 00:23:06.281
With your help and my
carefully crafted master plan.

480
00:23:06.282 --> 00:23:09.904
we'll find the fabled
lost Jewel of Atlantis

481
00:23:09.905 --> 00:23:14.078
and finally make me the
richest duck in the world!

482
00:23:14.079 --> 00:23:15.791
[Evil Laughter]

483
00:23:17.082 --> 00:23:19.754
But first. here are your company IDs.

484
00:23:19.755 --> 00:23:23.678
also good for 40% off life vest
rental in case of emergency.

485
00:23:23.679 --> 00:23:25.590
Gabby McStabberson.

486
00:23:25.591 --> 00:23:27.972
Hack and Slash Smashkinov.

487
00:23:27.973 --> 00:23:30.134
Donald Duck.

488
00:23:30.135 --> 00:23:31.596
Duck?

489
00:23:31.597 --> 00:23:33.478
Duck?!

490
00:23:33.479 --> 00:23:36.311
Ha! Now remember. bedtime is at 9:00.

491
00:23:36.312 --> 00:23:39.063
And no sugar after 7:00. Oh. and...

492
00:23:39.064 --> 00:23:41.736
I run a multi-trillion dollar business.

493
00:23:41.737 --> 00:23:43.938
I can handle a few
juveniles for the weekend.

494
00:23:43.939 --> 00:23:46.070
You just focus on this new job of yours.

495
00:23:46.071 --> 00:23:49.073
Besides. we've got a
pretty low-key day planned.

496
00:23:49.074 --> 00:23:50.905
Hoist the mainsail!

497
00:23:50.906 --> 00:23:54.038
Other boat words. to
Atlantis! Dive! Dive!

498
00:23:54.039 --> 00:23:56.290
- No. no. wait!
- Aye aye!

499
00:23:56.291 --> 00:24:01.046
Launchpad. the hatch. Stop the...

500
00:24:05.881 --> 00:24:07.052
Whoo-hoo!

501
00:24:09.595 --> 00:24:11.556
Talk to your uncle.

502
00:24:11.557 --> 00:24:13.057
Hey. Uncle Donald.

503
00:24:13.058 --> 00:24:14.599
Nope. yeah. pretty boring.

504
00:24:14.600 --> 00:24:16.212
We napped. rubbed
ointment on our joints.

505
00:24:16.215 --> 00:24:17.345
old people stuff.

506
00:24:17.348 --> 00:24:18.973
Oh. what about the dragon?

507
00:24:18.974 --> 00:24:20.314
And the plane crash?

508
00:24:20.315 --> 00:24:23.277
Whoops. 3:00 pm. Time for dinner. Bye!

509
00:24:23.278 --> 00:24:25.279
Why didn't you tell him the truth?

510
00:24:25.280 --> 00:24:27.281
You didn't tell your
grandma we were going

511
00:24:27.282 --> 00:24:29.193
to a dangerous underwater city. did you?

512
00:24:29.194 --> 00:24:32.003
I kinda sorta... didn't
tell her anything?

513
00:24:32.006 --> 00:24:34.025
Webby. that's irresponsible!

514
00:24:34.028 --> 00:24:35.750
She'll be worried sick!

515
00:24:35.751 --> 00:24:38.042
Call your grandma this instant

516
00:24:38.043 --> 00:24:41.376
and tell her that you are spending
the night at a friend's house. okay?

517
00:24:41.377 --> 00:24:44.420
Lying: It's the responsible thing to do.

518
00:24:47.172 --> 00:24:51.215
Launchpad. have you ever
piloted a sub before?

519
00:24:51.216 --> 00:24:53.177
I sunk a helicopter in a wave pool once.

520
00:24:53.178 --> 00:24:55.560
- Same thing?
- I've done more with less.

521
00:24:55.561 --> 00:24:59.103
No matter. I'm back!
Unchartered territory.

522
00:24:59.104 --> 00:25:01.145
Bold new discoveries!

523
00:25:01.146 --> 00:25:03.648
Hello. bingo!

524
00:25:03.649 --> 00:25:05.650
I love road trips!

525
00:25:05.651 --> 00:25:08.443
I've got snacks. a playlist
of traditional sea chanties.

526
00:25:08.444 --> 00:25:10.234
matching family road trip shirts!

527
00:25:10.235 --> 00:25:13.698
I appreciate the enthusiasm.
but there's no time.

528
00:25:13.699 --> 00:25:16.621
- But according to the travel itinerary...
- Boo!

529
00:25:16.622 --> 00:25:20.164
Adventure isn't about
planning. it's about doing!

530
00:25:20.165 --> 00:25:22.587
So. what can I be in charge of?

531
00:25:22.588 --> 00:25:23.708
- The buzzsaw arm?
- No!

532
00:25:23.709 --> 00:25:25.089
- Sonic cannons?
- No!

533
00:25:25.090 --> 00:25:26.881
Hyper-dense zero-point
energy missiles

534
00:25:26.882 --> 00:25:28.633
to pierce the scaly hide of a Kraken?!

535
00:25:28.634 --> 00:25:30.465
None of those things are real things!

536
00:25:30.466 --> 00:25:32.216
This is your first expedition.

537
00:25:32.217 --> 00:25:35.049
so just stand back and watch an old pro

538
00:25:35.050 --> 00:25:36.681
from a safe distance.

539
00:25:36.682 --> 00:25:39.143
So what is this submarine equipped with?

540
00:25:39.144 --> 00:25:40.555
[Whirs]

541
00:25:40.556 --> 00:25:42.016
Seatbelts.

542
00:25:42.017 --> 00:25:43.227
[Laughing]

543
00:25:43.228 --> 00:25:44.770
Ha! Good one.

544
00:25:46.003 --> 00:25:47.748
Classic Scrooge-Dewey banter.

545
00:25:47.758 --> 00:25:49.075
the seasoned-but-tired explorer

546
00:25:49.078 --> 00:25:51.098
passing the torch to his
cocky young successor.

547
00:25:51.101 --> 00:25:53.148
I'm pretty sure he doesn't
actually know our names.

548
00:25:53.151 --> 00:25:54.618
- I'm sorry. what?
- I think he called me her board ones.

549
00:25:54.620 --> 00:25:56.200
Don't be ridiculous!

550
00:25:56.201 --> 00:25:58.783
Hey. Scrooge! When are we
gonna set sail. Scrooge?

551
00:25:58.784 --> 00:26:00.575
In a moment. Sonny Jim.

552
00:26:00.576 --> 00:26:03.958
I will cram it down your throat.

553
00:26:03.959 --> 00:26:07.081
Guys. lighten up! We're
on a deep-sea expedition

554
00:26:07.082 --> 00:26:09.384
with Scrooge McDuck!

555
00:26:12.311 --> 00:26:15.219
Mr. McQuack. chart a course.

556
00:26:15.220 --> 00:26:20.184
Next stop. the lost City of Atlantis!

557
00:26:20.185 --> 00:26:21.596
[Cheering]

558
00:26:21.597 --> 00:26:24.559
At about 16:00 hours!

559
00:26:24.560 --> 00:26:26.982
Shanty time!

560
00:26:28.193 --> 00:26:29.564
♪ We love to sail the ocean ♪

561
00:26:29.565 --> 00:26:31.065
♪ We love to sail... ♪

562
00:26:31.066 --> 00:26:32.817
♪ Traveled all across the ocean ♪

563
00:26:32.818 --> 00:26:35.029
[Singing In German]

564
00:26:35.030 --> 00:26:38.162
♪ ...never have I been lucky ♪

565
00:26:38.163 --> 00:26:39.413
[Snoring]

566
00:26:39.414 --> 00:26:40.875
Driving! Piloting.

567
00:26:40.876 --> 00:26:43.619
Driving. right?

568
00:26:45.250 --> 00:26:47.291
Hey. Scrooge. First Mate Dewey here.

569
00:26:47.292 --> 00:26:49.043
Your map's got us going the long way.

570
00:26:49.044 --> 00:26:51.295
I can probably find a
shortcut if you just let me...

571
00:26:51.296 --> 00:26:53.798
Uh-uh. lad. The shortest
distance between two points

572
00:26:53.799 --> 00:26:55.760
isn't always a straight line.

573
00:26:55.761 --> 00:26:59.283
Okay. but yes. it is.
so if you just go...

574
00:27:03.268 --> 00:27:06.140
[Snoring]

575
00:27:06.141 --> 00:27:07.352
Driving!

576
00:27:12.107 --> 00:27:13.407
[Beep]

577
00:27:13.408 --> 00:27:14.780
Huh?

578
00:27:16.782 --> 00:27:18.112
Shortcut achieved!

579
00:27:18.113 --> 00:27:20.154
He'll thank me later.

580
00:27:20.155 --> 00:27:22.617
[Screaming]

581
00:27:22.618 --> 00:27:26.210
[Roaring]

582
00:27:26.211 --> 00:27:29.123
Oh. you kids'll be the death of me.

583
00:27:29.124 --> 00:27:33.168
Dewey! Dewey will be the death of you!

584
00:27:34.219 --> 00:27:36.050
Can we make a pit stop?

585
00:27:36.051 --> 00:27:38.092
I have to use the
bathroom. but it's. um...

586
00:27:38.093 --> 00:27:39.433
Occupied?

587
00:27:39.434 --> 00:27:41.636
For the love of... It's
the middle of the ocean!

588
00:27:41.637 --> 00:27:43.517
There are no pit stops.

589
00:27:43.518 --> 00:27:46.310
How 'bout that conspicuously
unmarked tanker?

590
00:27:46.311 --> 00:27:49.774
Ah. little Dewey's first steps.

591
00:27:49.775 --> 00:27:51.776
And that's Huey in the playoffs.

592
00:27:51.777 --> 00:27:53.188
He was the waterboy.

593
00:27:55.190 --> 00:27:59.283
Oh. look! That's us
climbing the Grand Canyon...

594
00:27:59.284 --> 00:28:02.116
display at the supermarket. Ah...

595
00:28:02.117 --> 00:28:04.699
Ah. I miss them so much.

596
00:28:04.700 --> 00:28:06.871
but we need this job.

597
00:28:06.872 --> 00:28:09.373
So. tell me about your family.

598
00:28:09.374 --> 00:28:11.335
I was raised by warrior monks

599
00:28:11.336 --> 00:28:13.799
who spoke only the
language of the blade.

600
00:28:17.092 --> 00:28:18.342
Uh...

601
00:28:18.343 --> 00:28:19.514
[Beeping]

602
00:28:20.636 --> 00:28:21.807
We've got intruders!

603
00:28:23.428 --> 00:28:26.220
Scrooge?! What is he doing here?

604
00:28:26.221 --> 00:28:27.772
Strange weather patterns

605
00:28:27.773 --> 00:28:30.224
in a mysterious location
near treasure. Ha ha!

606
00:28:30.225 --> 00:28:32.316
I knew he couldn't resist!

607
00:28:32.317 --> 00:28:35.189
Hack. triangulate their sub's course!

608
00:28:35.190 --> 00:28:36.651
We'll tail Scrooge

609
00:28:36.652 --> 00:28:39.193
and steal the jewel out from under him!

610
00:28:39.194 --> 00:28:40.825
The boys?!

611
00:28:40.826 --> 00:28:43.577
Why. you get your hands... [Squawking]

612
00:28:43.578 --> 00:28:45.830
I'm gonna kill him!

613
00:28:45.831 --> 00:28:47.451
Ooh. better idea!

614
00:28:47.452 --> 00:28:50.044
Nab the jewel and kill them all!

615
00:28:50.045 --> 00:28:53.377
Somebody's angling for
employee of the month.

616
00:28:53.378 --> 00:28:56.171
[Laughing]

617
00:28:58.053 --> 00:29:02.216
[Thunder Crashing]

618
00:29:02.217 --> 00:29:03.387
♪ ♪

619
00:29:03.388 --> 00:29:05.760
SCROOGE: The Drake Barrier Reef.

620
00:29:05.761 --> 00:29:08.352
Powerful currents
combined with rocky terrain

621
00:29:08.353 --> 00:29:11.355
make it nearly impossible to navigate.

622
00:29:11.356 --> 00:29:14.519
but on that rare
occasion when snow falls

623
00:29:14.522 --> 00:29:16.861
above the reef. the currents cool.

624
00:29:16.862 --> 00:29:20.324
allowing safe passage to...

625
00:29:20.325 --> 00:29:21.325
[Snoring. Startling]

626
00:29:21.326 --> 00:29:22.667
Are we there yet?

627
00:29:22.670 --> 00:29:24.699
- I was just about to...
- Right side or the left side?

628
00:29:24.700 --> 00:29:26.951
- If you'd just let me...
- Look! There that thing is!

629
00:29:26.952 --> 00:29:28.123
We found it!

630
00:29:33.418 --> 00:29:35.499
Whoa!

631
00:29:35.500 --> 00:29:37.551
Yes. good. Atlantis.

632
00:29:37.552 --> 00:29:40.094
"Ooh! Aah!"

633
00:29:40.095 --> 00:29:41.886
Thanks for spoiling the moment.

634
00:29:41.887 --> 00:29:44.298
The whole place is upside down!

635
00:29:44.299 --> 00:29:46.431
Oh. well. that's a new one.

636
00:29:56.021 --> 00:29:57.192
Whoa!

637
00:30:03.949 --> 00:30:06.280
Just call your grandma
already! It's no big deal.

638
00:30:06.281 --> 00:30:07.321
[Dialing]

639
00:30:07.322 --> 00:30:08.913
Aah!

640
00:30:08.914 --> 00:30:10.955
Remember. you're at a
friend's house. okay?

641
00:30:10.956 --> 00:30:12.496
You got this.

642
00:30:12.497 --> 00:30:14.328
[Rapidly] Hi. Granny.
I'm spending the night

643
00:30:14.329 --> 00:30:15.920
at a friend's house so nothing is wrong!

644
00:30:15.921 --> 00:30:17.541
Oh. you don't got this.

645
00:30:17.542 --> 00:30:21.545
Ah-ha! Well. according
to these markings.

646
00:30:21.546 --> 00:30:23.217
the Atlantines were so eager

647
00:30:23.218 --> 00:30:26.260
to build an epic city of
wonders and death traps.

648
00:30:26.261 --> 00:30:29.103
they didn't stop to figure
out a proper support structure.

649
00:30:29.104 --> 00:30:31.185
and the whole thing fell into the sea!

650
00:30:31.186 --> 00:30:33.607
You kids best stay by the
sub while I scout ahead.

651
00:30:33.608 --> 00:30:35.810
Dewey ran in as soon as
you said "death traps."

652
00:30:35.811 --> 00:30:37.942
DEWEY: Come on. Scrooge! We got this.

653
00:30:37.943 --> 00:30:41.316
Boy! [Sighs. Mutters]

654
00:30:44.950 --> 00:30:46.450
- [Blade Rings]
- [Donald Squawks]

655
00:30:46.451 --> 00:30:48.122
Oopsie!

656
00:30:48.123 --> 00:30:49.123
[Grunts]

657
00:30:49.124 --> 00:30:51.325
Hmm?

658
00:30:51.326 --> 00:30:52.627
Meh.

659
00:30:54.709 --> 00:30:56.961
You made me miss!

660
00:30:56.962 --> 00:31:00.464
Uh... if we get rid of them now.

661
00:31:00.465 --> 00:31:03.047
we can't torture them later!

662
00:31:03.048 --> 00:31:06.050
Brilliant! I want Scrooge alive

663
00:31:06.051 --> 00:31:10.054
when I shove the Jewel of
Atlantis in his smug face!

664
00:31:10.055 --> 00:31:12.726
He thinks his so rich and so Scottish.

665
00:31:12.727 --> 00:31:16.561
but I'm wearing a kilt. McDuck. a kilt!

666
00:31:20.565 --> 00:31:22.526
Dah! Lad!

667
00:31:22.527 --> 00:31:25.449
I thought the traps
would get you for sure!

668
00:31:25.450 --> 00:31:26.991
[Whirring]

669
00:31:26.992 --> 00:31:29.113
Stupid upside-down temple!

670
00:31:29.114 --> 00:31:31.455
Nothing cool about
walking under buzzsaws!

671
00:31:31.456 --> 00:31:36.411
From now on. don't touch anything!

672
00:31:38.373 --> 00:31:39.915
[Grunts]

673
00:31:44.129 --> 00:31:45.800
[Screaming]

674
00:31:47.472 --> 00:31:48.632
[Cracks Spine]

675
00:31:48.633 --> 00:31:51.555
Maybe Atlantis was an
ambitious first outing.

676
00:31:51.556 --> 00:31:52.766
[Ringing]

677
00:31:52.767 --> 00:31:53.767
[Grunting]

678
00:31:53.768 --> 00:31:55.139
Hi again. Granny!

679
00:31:55.140 --> 00:31:57.141
Still at a friend's house.

680
00:31:57.142 --> 00:32:00.194
Uh. her name? Sub... ina!

681
00:32:00.195 --> 00:32:03.397
A totally real name for
a definitely real person!

682
00:32:03.398 --> 00:32:04.648
[Beep]

683
00:32:04.649 --> 00:32:05.900
Uh. good try.

684
00:32:05.901 --> 00:32:08.492
- [Grunts]
- Launchpad. are you okay?

685
00:32:08.493 --> 00:32:09.653
[Mumbling]

686
00:32:09.654 --> 00:32:13.448
Ah. a little snake venom
never... [Gibbering]

687
00:32:14.950 --> 00:32:16.024
Hi. nice to meet you!

688
00:32:16.027 --> 00:32:17.868
I'm everybody's friend!

689
00:32:17.871 --> 00:32:20.164
[Screaming]

690
00:32:20.165 --> 00:32:23.377
Um. I've got to go to the bathroom.

691
00:32:23.378 --> 00:32:25.549
I'll be right back!

692
00:32:25.550 --> 00:32:27.841
[Groaning]

693
00:32:27.842 --> 00:32:29.134
[Grunts]

694
00:32:30.465 --> 00:32:32.726
Whoa!

695
00:32:32.727 --> 00:32:36.020
Suspension bridge? Chasm?
Glowing blue mystical lasers?

696
00:32:36.021 --> 00:32:38.142
Classic!

697
00:32:38.143 --> 00:32:40.735
[Muttering] ...Scrooge. Wait
till I get my hands on him.

698
00:32:45.480 --> 00:32:49.982
Even a basic death trap still
has the word "death" in the title.

699
00:32:51.196 --> 00:32:53.949
[Squawking]

700
00:32:59.044 --> 00:33:00.164
Oh. no.

701
00:33:00.165 --> 00:33:01.359
We'll find another route.

702
00:33:01.362 --> 00:33:03.533
It's not safe for amateur adventurers.

703
00:33:03.536 --> 00:33:05.499
That sounds like a challenge!

704
00:33:05.500 --> 00:33:08.382
I have to stress that
is not a challenge.

705
00:33:08.383 --> 00:33:11.005
Is exactly what you say to
dissuade the weak of heart

706
00:33:11.006 --> 00:33:12.806
from accepting the challenge!

707
00:33:12.807 --> 00:33:14.388
Well. challenge accepted!

708
00:33:14.389 --> 00:33:15.720
There's no challenge!

709
00:33:17.182 --> 00:33:18.773
Dewey!

710
00:33:20.685 --> 00:33:22.146
♪ Dew... ♪

711
00:33:22.147 --> 00:33:23.517
[Screaming]

712
00:33:23.518 --> 00:33:25.689
♪ Dewey. Dewey. Dewey. Dewey ♪

713
00:33:25.690 --> 00:33:27.481
Huh? Aah!

714
00:33:27.482 --> 00:33:28.902
♪ Dew. uh. Dewey. Dewey. Dewey ♪

715
00:33:28.903 --> 00:33:30.654
[Quacks. Screams]

716
00:33:30.655 --> 00:33:31.695
♪ Dew ♪

717
00:33:31.696 --> 00:33:32.826
Oh. no!

718
00:33:32.827 --> 00:33:34.158
♪ How does he Dewey it? ♪

719
00:33:34.159 --> 00:33:35.159
♪ I don't know ♪

720
00:33:35.160 --> 00:33:38.242
[Riffing]

721
00:33:38.243 --> 00:33:40.454
[Quacking]

722
00:33:40.455 --> 00:33:43.588
♪ Dew! And now you know ♪

723
00:33:45.670 --> 00:33:48.423
Nailed it!

724
00:33:53.098 --> 00:33:55.889
Sure. if you want to do it the easy way.

725
00:33:55.890 --> 00:33:58.602
Why wouldn't you want
to do it the easy way?

726
00:33:58.603 --> 00:34:01.765
You've got to work
smarter. lad. not harder.

727
00:34:01.766 --> 00:34:02.766
Aah!

728
00:34:02.767 --> 00:34:04.438
Ugh. "lad."

729
00:34:04.439 --> 00:34:07.771
I don't call you "old
man" or "Scotty McTophat."

730
00:34:07.772 --> 00:34:09.113
Respect your elder.

731
00:34:09.114 --> 00:34:10.904
When you adventure
with Scrooge McDuck...

732
00:34:10.905 --> 00:34:12.176
But I'm not.

733
00:34:12.179 --> 00:34:14.618
You want me to adventure
behind Scrooge McDuck.

734
00:34:14.619 --> 00:34:15.990
or wait by the sub!

735
00:34:15.991 --> 00:34:18.122
I might as well be
back on the houseboat!

736
00:34:18.123 --> 00:34:20.534
Because you have no
idea what you're doing!

737
00:34:20.535 --> 00:34:21.461
So show me!

738
00:34:21.464 --> 00:34:23.055
Give me a chance instead of lumping us

739
00:34:23.058 --> 00:34:25.169
all together in the back
seat while you drive!

740
00:34:25.170 --> 00:34:27.711
I'm not lumping you all together.

741
00:34:27.712 --> 00:34:28.962
Oh. really?

742
00:34:28.963 --> 00:34:29.963
Which triplet am I?

743
00:34:29.964 --> 00:34:34.218
It's... Bluey?

744
00:34:34.219 --> 00:34:36.141
Aah! Ow!

745
00:34:39.644 --> 00:34:42.056
Ugh! Fantastic.

746
00:34:42.057 --> 00:34:45.059
You see what I'm talking about?

747
00:34:45.060 --> 00:34:46.730
You four find another way 'round!

748
00:34:46.731 --> 00:34:49.693
We're going to... push onward.

749
00:34:49.694 --> 00:34:51.985
apparently.

750
00:34:51.986 --> 00:34:54.278
[Grunting]

751
00:34:54.279 --> 00:34:56.990
[Sighs]

752
00:34:56.991 --> 00:34:59.953
Why. this is no bathroom!

753
00:34:59.954 --> 00:35:02.786
This shortcuts leads right
to the treasure chamber!

754
00:35:02.787 --> 00:35:05.169
I don't even know why
I hired the rest of you!

755
00:35:05.170 --> 00:35:06.381
Help him up!

756
00:35:08.833 --> 00:35:13.678
Ow. Ouch! Owie! Owie!

757
00:35:16.891 --> 00:35:20.054
Maybe I could just hire some family.

758
00:35:20.055 --> 00:35:22.637
Then they'd have to listen to me.

759
00:35:25.480 --> 00:35:30.234
[Laughs] There she is.
the Jewel of Atlantis!

760
00:35:30.235 --> 00:35:32.776
[Cackling]

761
00:35:32.777 --> 00:35:36.030
- Who's that?
- Flintheart Glomgold.

762
00:35:36.031 --> 00:35:38.612
the poor man's version of me.

763
00:35:38.613 --> 00:35:41.655
which. to be fair. still
makes him insanely rich.

764
00:35:41.656 --> 00:35:43.577
[Cackling]

765
00:35:43.578 --> 00:35:44.658
Load up the sub.

766
00:35:44.659 --> 00:35:46.500
They've got Uncle Donald?

767
00:35:46.501 --> 00:35:47.622
What?

768
00:35:50.165 --> 00:35:52.756
Let go of my uncle!

769
00:35:52.757 --> 00:35:55.510
- No.
- I wasn't prepared for that.

770
00:35:59.724 --> 00:36:01.805
What are you doing here. Flinty?

771
00:36:01.806 --> 00:36:03.887
What are you doing here. Scrooge?

772
00:36:03.888 --> 00:36:06.180
I told you to keep the boys safe!

773
00:36:06.181 --> 00:36:07.851
Ah. they're perfectly fine.

774
00:36:07.852 --> 00:36:09.893
Oh. yeah? Where are the other two?

775
00:36:09.894 --> 00:36:12.146
Back safe in the room with
the fire and the snakes.

776
00:36:12.147 --> 00:36:14.738
- What?
- Ah. Scroogy.

777
00:36:14.739 --> 00:36:17.111
I see you know my newest employee.

778
00:36:17.112 --> 00:36:21.325
Your new job is with my sworn enemy?

779
00:36:21.326 --> 00:36:24.868
I can't keep track of
all your sworn enemies!

780
00:36:24.869 --> 00:36:28.372
Now. now. Donald has
been a model employee.

781
00:36:28.373 --> 00:36:30.874
and an excellent prisoner.

782
00:36:30.875 --> 00:36:32.877
Yeah! Wait. what?

783
00:36:36.711 --> 00:36:39.803
Hiring my own nephew in
order to use him against me?

784
00:36:39.804 --> 00:36:41.596
Now. that is good planning.

785
00:36:47.142 --> 00:36:49.773
Have fun being the second
richest duck in the world...

786
00:36:49.774 --> 00:36:52.146
for the next five minutes.

787
00:36:52.147 --> 00:36:54.819
[Cackling]

788
00:36:58.693 --> 00:37:02.237
I'd like to point out that
this trap was not my fault.

789
00:37:03.561 --> 00:37:05.909
Junior Woodchuck Rule 841:

790
00:37:05.910 --> 00:37:08.542
There's always another way around.

791
00:37:08.543 --> 00:37:09.833
Hup!

792
00:37:09.834 --> 00:37:11.205
- [Ringing]
- Hup!

793
00:37:11.206 --> 00:37:12.416
Oh. no. no. no. no!

794
00:37:12.417 --> 00:37:14.208
Oh. look! Uncle Hampus is here.

795
00:37:14.209 --> 00:37:16.130
and he only speaks Swedish.

796
00:37:16.131 --> 00:37:18.962
We don't want to be
rude. so... good-bye?

797
00:37:18.963 --> 00:37:20.438
And you're done.

798
00:37:20.441 --> 00:37:22.760
Yeah. you're never gonna
be able to back up that lie.

799
00:37:22.763 --> 00:37:23.883
That was crazy!

800
00:37:23.886 --> 00:37:25.429
Whoa!

801
00:37:25.430 --> 00:37:26.890
Oh. hej. Beakley!

802
00:37:26.891 --> 00:37:29.763
Subina... [Speaking Swedish]

803
00:37:29.764 --> 00:37:31.685
[Glomgold Cackling]

804
00:37:31.686 --> 00:37:34.228
Take 'em down!

805
00:37:34.229 --> 00:37:35.360
Ojda.

806
00:37:36.544 --> 00:37:38.546
We gotta stop the water!

807
00:37:44.577 --> 00:37:47.619
[Quacking]

808
00:37:47.622 --> 00:37:48.663
Oh. no.

809
00:37:53.208 --> 00:37:55.499
[Sighs] I knew it!

810
00:37:55.500 --> 00:37:57.703
I knew I couldn't
trust you with the boys!

811
00:37:57.706 --> 00:37:58.842
Not the time. Donald.

812
00:37:58.843 --> 00:38:00.594
Crazy old man!

813
00:38:00.595 --> 00:38:03.006
All you care about is
your next adventure.

814
00:38:03.007 --> 00:38:06.099
This is the Spear of
Selene all over again!

815
00:38:06.100 --> 00:38:09.563
I was not responsible
for the Spear of Selene!

816
00:38:09.564 --> 00:38:13.267
Stop! Scrooge was trying
to keep me out of trouble.

817
00:38:13.268 --> 00:38:15.264
but I was so caught up in...

818
00:38:15.267 --> 00:38:16.770
Why is there a lamp on the floor?

819
00:38:16.771 --> 00:38:17.981
What?

820
00:38:17.982 --> 00:38:19.863
Atlantis is upside down.

821
00:38:19.864 --> 00:38:22.236
That means that lamp was
supposed to be on the floor

822
00:38:22.237 --> 00:38:23.947
surrounded by all this treasure.

823
00:38:23.948 --> 00:38:25.909
Attaboy. lad. Keep going.

824
00:38:25.910 --> 00:38:29.032
But why would you surround that
thing with treasure unless...

825
00:38:29.033 --> 00:38:32.876
BOTH: That's the real Jewel of Atlantis!

826
00:38:32.877 --> 00:38:34.998
That thing lit up when
the trap was sprung.

827
00:38:34.999 --> 00:38:38.882
I bet my bottom dollar it's the
power source that runs the city!

828
00:38:38.883 --> 00:38:41.215
Uncle Donald. you
gotta let the room flood

829
00:38:41.216 --> 00:38:42.336
so I can grab the jewel.

830
00:38:42.337 --> 00:38:43.677
That's crazy!

831
00:38:43.678 --> 00:38:46.260
I'm supposed to. what. let go?

832
00:38:46.261 --> 00:38:47.721
Trust you?

833
00:38:47.722 --> 00:38:50.844
Well. yeah. that's
kind of all you can do.

834
00:38:50.845 --> 00:38:53.808
This is a surprisingly
insightful death trap!

835
00:39:05.990 --> 00:39:07.362
[Quacks]

836
00:39:13.515 --> 00:39:16.251
[Grunting]

837
00:39:25.930 --> 00:39:28.383
[Panting]

838
00:39:29.974 --> 00:39:32.807
Hey! We're gonna be okay!

839
00:39:34.098 --> 00:39:36.149
[Grunting]

840
00:39:36.150 --> 00:39:39.102
[Screaming]

841
00:39:39.103 --> 00:39:43.156
Oh. yeah. those guys.

842
00:39:43.157 --> 00:39:45.989
Huey and Louie!

843
00:39:45.990 --> 00:39:48.071
Are doing okay!

844
00:39:48.072 --> 00:39:50.284
[Grunting]

845
00:39:50.285 --> 00:39:52.956
Wait! Where's Glomgold?

846
00:39:52.957 --> 00:39:54.195
[Walkie-Talkie Crackles]

847
00:39:54.198 --> 00:39:56.710
GLOMGOLD: Hey. team. Wanted to thank you

848
00:39:56.711 --> 00:39:58.081
for keeping Scrooge's kin busy

849
00:39:58.082 --> 00:40:00.526
while I escape with the
jewel and blow up Atlantis

850
00:40:00.529 --> 00:40:03.006
with my most hated rival inside.

851
00:40:03.007 --> 00:40:06.009
But I thought employees were
greatest treasure of all!

852
00:40:06.010 --> 00:40:07.130
Don't be ridiculous!

853
00:40:07.131 --> 00:40:08.922
Treasure is the
greatest treasure of all.

854
00:40:08.923 --> 00:40:11.686
That's why it's called
treasure! Glomgold out!

855
00:40:12.977 --> 00:40:14.559
We have to go!

856
00:40:20.775 --> 00:40:22.105
- Huh?
- Mr. Duck.

857
00:40:22.106 --> 00:40:24.509
Could we. um. maybe bum a ride with you?

858
00:40:34.118 --> 00:40:36.750
That was some quick thinking.

859
00:40:36.751 --> 00:40:39.834
You just may be an
adventurer yet. Dewey.

860
00:40:42.417 --> 00:40:46.460
[Reporters Clamoring]

861
00:40:46.461 --> 00:40:48.962
Aye. aye. Okay. Settle down.

862
00:40:48.963 --> 00:40:52.395
Ha ha! Ladies and
gentlemen of the press.

863
00:40:52.398 --> 00:40:57.310
it is with great pride that I.
Flintheart Glomgold. present...

864
00:40:57.311 --> 00:41:00.434
The Jewel of Atlantis!

865
00:41:00.435 --> 00:41:01.525
What?!

866
00:41:01.526 --> 00:41:03.276
Is that Scrooge McDuck?

867
00:41:03.277 --> 00:41:06.320
- Mr. McDuck...
- [Clamor Resumes]

868
00:41:07.982 --> 00:41:10.614
An efficient. clean source of energy

869
00:41:10.615 --> 00:41:13.747
that could power Duckburg for 50 years.

870
00:41:13.748 --> 00:41:17.621
courtesy of your friends at
McDuck Water and Electric.

871
00:41:17.622 --> 00:41:19.953
Ooh. Mr. McDuck. how do you respond

872
00:41:19.954 --> 00:41:22.416
to claims by other Scottish billionaires

873
00:41:22.417 --> 00:41:24.127
that they have the real jewel?

874
00:41:24.128 --> 00:41:25.839
That bauble?

875
00:41:25.840 --> 00:41:28.802
That's nice. but it's
obviously super cursed.

876
00:41:28.803 --> 00:41:30.053
No. it's not!

877
00:41:30.054 --> 00:41:31.425
[Splashing]

878
00:41:31.426 --> 00:41:34.347
[Roaring]

879
00:41:34.348 --> 00:41:38.182
[Screams] Curse you. McDuck!

880
00:41:41.600 --> 00:41:45.188
- Webby. Uncle Hampus.
- How long?

881
00:41:45.189 --> 00:41:46.400
Whole time.

882
00:41:46.401 --> 00:41:48.942
Granny. I can explain.

883
00:41:48.943 --> 00:41:52.486
Dear. you are safer in a
sunken city with Scrooge McDuck

884
00:41:52.487 --> 00:41:55.198
than you are locked in
a vault in Fort Knox.

885
00:41:55.199 --> 00:41:57.411
No more lies...

886
00:41:57.412 --> 00:41:59.414
and you can go with
him wherever you like.

887
00:42:02.206 --> 00:42:04.297
- Now. Donald. don't...
- Stop.

888
00:42:04.298 --> 00:42:07.466
I admit I'm a little overprotective.

889
00:42:07.469 --> 00:42:08.753
LOUIE: A little?!

890
00:42:10.094 --> 00:42:11.425
No matter what I do.

891
00:42:11.426 --> 00:42:13.677
these boys will get into trouble.

892
00:42:13.678 --> 00:42:18.101
so maybe you could teach them
how to get out of trouble.

893
00:42:18.102 --> 00:42:19.222
Uncle Donald?

894
00:42:19.223 --> 00:42:20.401
It might be okay

895
00:42:20.414 --> 00:42:23.266
if the boys saw you
every once in a while.

896
00:42:23.267 --> 00:42:25.018
[Cheering]

897
00:42:25.019 --> 00:42:29.022
Sometimes. like birthdays
or federal holidays.

898
00:42:29.023 --> 00:42:30.985
- Nothing too...
- [Bang]

899
00:42:33.828 --> 00:42:37.200
Ooh! I may have left the
engine running in the houseboat.

900
00:42:37.201 --> 00:42:41.034
I may have a dozen or so spare bedrooms

901
00:42:41.035 --> 00:42:43.837
in the mansion.

902
00:42:43.838 --> 00:42:45.378
[Chuckles]

903
00:42:45.379 --> 00:42:47.171
[Cheering]

904
00:42:50.004 --> 00:42:51.465
There you have it.

905
00:42:51.466 --> 00:42:55.008
Reclusive adventure capitalist
Scrooge McDuck is back.

906
00:42:55.009 --> 00:42:56.552
with family in tow.

907
00:42:56.555 --> 00:43:00.143
solving mysteries and rewriting history.

908
00:43:00.144 --> 00:43:03.226
DONALD: Easy. A little to the left.

909
00:43:03.227 --> 00:43:05.018
No. no. no. no!

910
00:43:05.019 --> 00:43:07.020
Did I do it good?

911
00:43:07.021 --> 00:43:09.773
[Laughter]

912
00:43:09.774 --> 00:43:10.945
[Screams]

913
00:43:30.505 --> 00:43:32.507
Mom?

914
00:43:33.067 --> 00:43:38.745
- <font color="#D81D1D">Synced and corrected by VitoSilans</font> -
-- <font color="#138CE9">www.Addic7ed.com</font> --

915
00:44:08.279 --> 00:44:11.114
[Panting]

916
00:44:11.116 --> 00:44:13.182
Take that!
[Laughing]

917
00:44:16.321 --> 00:44:20.423
Dewey. don't yell at your target
before you fire.

918
00:44:20.425 --> 00:44:24.160
You'll lose the element
of surprise.

919
00:44:24.162 --> 00:44:26.696
-<i> You'd better duck.</i>
- [Yelling]

920
00:44:26.698 --> 00:44:30.199
- Ahh! [Grunts]
- [Laughter]

921
00:44:30.201 --> 00:44:32.135
<i>"DuckTales."</i>
